<title>BELGIUM: Bangemann says did not criticise EP report.</title>
<headline>Bangemann says did not criticise EP report.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Commissioner Martin Bangemann did not criticise a European Parliament inquiry committee report into mad cow disease as stated in a Reuter story on Friday, his spokesman said.</p>
<p>Jochen Kubosch noted that statements by Bangemann in a written interview were made before the parliament had drafted its report.</p>
<p>He said that Bangemann fully shared the position announced by Commission President Jacques Santer to the committee of inquiry last month.</p>
<p>Santer told the panel that the Commission's veterinary and public health services needed to be reorganised.</p>
</text>
